    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the on-demand cross-reference query
                (`listing/xrefs.rs`), the data-reference projection.

    The Listing tier and the xref query it feeds are built ONLY on the
    real-object bootstrap path, never on this XML binaryimage path
    (docs/spec/01-program-prep.md section 1.6), which is exactly why the parity
    oracle is structurally untouched by this change.  This case pins that the
    XML path renders as before.

    The end-to-end proof (the prompt, the banner, the thunked trailer and the
    global all resolved, and the clobbering function still claiming nothing)
    needs a real 32-bit PIC object and lives in the cargo gate
    `decompiler/crates/kuna-console/tests/verify_picbase.rs`, over the
    `picbase_i386` fixture.

    Reuses the GH-558 bytes as a small, deterministic loadable function.

